at no charge, which is the amazing.

00:30:31.880 --> 00:30:34.800
>> What's the one lie that entrepreneurs

00:30:33.400 --> 00:30:35.800
tell themselves that holds them back

00:30:34.800 --> 00:30:38.040
from success?

00:30:35.800 --> 00:30:40.560
>> I would say that lie would be playing it

00:30:38.040 --> 00:30:43.960
too small. So, not dreaming big enough,

00:30:40.560 --> 00:30:45.960
not having a massive goal. I think a lot

00:30:43.960 --> 00:30:47.400
of entrepreneurs, they they have very

00:30:45.960 --> 00:30:48.880
small goals. Whereas, if they had a

00:30:47.400 --> 00:30:49.760
bigger goal, if they started thinking

00:30:48.880 --> 00:30:51.040
from the beginning, "Hey, I'm going to

00:30:49.760 --> 00:30:52.680
build an empire. I'm going to do 10

00:30:51.040 --> 00:30:54.600
stores. I'm going to do 100 stores."

00:30:52.680 --> 00:30:56.400
Whatever their goal is, that's going to

00:30:54.600 --> 00:30:57.360
help them get there a lot faster.

00:30:56.400 --> 00:30:58.680
>> Mhm. Do you have a goal-setting

00:30:57.360 --> 00:31:00.000
structure that you'd like to give to the

00:30:58.680 --> 00:31:00.440
audience here that entrepreneurs should

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:02.640
take?

00:31:00.440 --> 00:31:04.920
>> I think that it really depends on

00:31:02.640 --> 00:31:07.040
everyone's mindset. I think if you have

00:31:04.920 --> 00:31:09.320
an appetite and you're hungry for for

00:31:07.040 --> 00:31:10.600
something big, dream big. If you believe

00:31:09.320 --> 00:31:13.120
it and you have that unshakeable

00:31:10.600 --> 00:31:14.920
confidence, then go for it. But, if you

00:31:13.120 --> 00:31:16.280
need something that is more realistic

00:31:14.920 --> 00:31:18.320
and it happens to be smaller, that's

00:31:16.280 --> 00:31:19.800
that's totally fine as long as it pushes

00:31:18.320 --> 00:31:22.560
you. Because ultimately, if you don't

00:31:19.800 --> 00:31:24.800
hit your goal 100%, but you get 80% of

00:31:22.560 --> 00:31:26.440
it, if your goal is big, that 80%,

00:31:24.800 --> 00:31:27.760
that's still going to be amazing

00:31:26.440 --> 00:31:30.000
success.

00:31:27.760 --> 00:31:31.840
>> So, you said that nutrition drives 80%

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:33.880
of results, not workouts. How does that

00:31:31.840 --> 00:31:34.400
insight drive Pure Green Marketing

00:31:33.880 --> 00:31:36.560
strategy?

00:31:34.400 --> 00:31:38.360
>> Sure. So, what we did was we built this

00:31:36.560 --> 00:31:40.000
nutritional advisory board with four

00:31:38.360 --> 00:31:42.360
dieticians, three from professional

00:31:40.000 --> 00:31:44.320
sports teams, one from the US military.

00:31:42.360 --> 00:31:46.320
And they back up everything that we do

00:31:44.320 --> 00:31:47.760
with peer-reviewed scientific research.

00:31:46.320 --> 00:31:49.840
If there's an a new ingredient that we

00:31:47.760 --> 00:31:52.400
want to use, we run it by them and they

00:31:49.840 --> 00:31:54.560
send us all the research and tell us if

00:31:52.400 --> 00:31:57.160
it's approved or it's not approved. By

00:31:54.560 --> 00:31:58.120
focusing on nutrition, by being very

00:31:57.160 --> 00:32:00.400
transparent, so if you go on our

00:31:58.120 --> 00:32:02.680
website, you click on any product, it'll

00:32:00.400 --> 00:32:04.960
show you the full extended nutrition

00:32:02.680 --> 00:32:06.960
panel. Any claim that we make is backed

00:32:04.960 --> 00:32:10.200
up and cited with that peer-reviewed

00:32:06.960 --> 00:32:12.520
scientific research. So, that 80%

00:32:10.200 --> 00:32:13.840
nutrition drives everything that we do.

00:32:12.520 --> 00:32:15.760
>> You'll have big bets, you'll have small

00:32:13.840 --> 00:32:17.080
bets. Not all bets pay off. For you,

00:32:15.760 --> 00:32:18.600
what was the number one marketing

00:32:17.080 --> 00:32:19.080
strategy that was a total waste of

00:32:18.600 --> 00:32:22.360
money?

00:32:19.080 --> 00:32:25.280
>> For us, very recently, we spent a ton of

00:32:22.360 --> 00:32:26.760
money pumped into Meta and Google for

00:32:25.280 --> 00:32:28.640
all of our franchise partners. We just

00:32:26.760 --> 00:32:30.480
wanted to pump it for them. And what we

00:32:28.640 --> 00:32:32.320
found is the return on ad spend was

00:32:30.480 --> 00:32:34.400
really lacking. Like, it was not worth

00:32:32.320 --> 00:32:36.040
it. And we think that it has its place.

00:32:34.400 --> 00:32:38.280
So, for new store openings, building

00:32:36.040 --> 00:32:40.360
that hype, it could be very helpful.

00:32:38.280 --> 00:32:41.880
When you have like a super something

00:32:40.360 --> 00:32:43.800
really special and unique, it could be

00:32:41.880 --> 00:32:46.760
helpful to get the word out. But just as

00:32:43.800 --> 00:32:48.880
a consistent part of marketing spend,

00:32:46.760 --> 00:32:51.560
it's only good for brand presence,

00:32:48.880 --> 00:32:53.560
really, but not to have constantly on.

00:32:51.560 --> 00:32:55.920
We've We've invested a lot of money

00:32:53.560 --> 00:32:58.520
testing it out and just doesn't work to

00:32:55.920 --> 00:33:00.000
drive traffic consistently to stores.

00:32:58.520 --> 00:33:01.720
>> What's the biggest red flag you look for

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:04.520
in potential franchisees?

00:33:01.720 --> 00:33:05.800
>> Biggest red flag is when they say, "I'm

00:33:04.520 --> 00:33:08.560
not going to run the store. I view this

00:33:05.800 --> 00:33:10.880
as a passive investment." Then

00:33:08.560 --> 00:33:12.920
that that's such a red flag because for

00:33:10.880 --> 00:33:15.200
us, we're looking for franchise partners

00:33:12.920 --> 00:33:17.160
that are owner-operators, that are

00:33:15.200 --> 00:33:18.520
willing in the early stages from grand

00:33:17.160 --> 00:33:19.480
opening, they're willing to do what it

00:33:18.520 --> 00:33:21.760
takes. They're willing to be in the

00:33:19.480 --> 00:33:23.720
store, build a great team, build that

00:33:21.760 --> 00:33:25.240
store culture. Then after a certain

00:33:23.720 --> 00:33:27.200
point, sometimes it takes a month, a

00:33:25.240 --> 00:33:28.960
couple of months, sometimes longer. Once

00:33:27.200 --> 00:33:32.040
that store culture is built, this

00:33:28.960 --> 00:33:34.600
becomes very duplicatable. Then that

00:33:32.040 --> 00:33:36.200
franchise partner is able to scale.

00:33:34.600 --> 00:33:38.080
They're able to hire a team lead or

00:33:36.200 --> 00:33:40.200
manager to then run day-to-day

00:33:38.080 --> 00:33:42.360
operations, and then they go on and

00:33:40.200 --> 00:33:44.640
duplicate the process. But when up

00:33:42.360 --> 00:33:46.960
front, they're ready to just hire

00:33:44.640 --> 00:33:47.600
someone to run it for them, that's not

00:33:46.960 --> 00:33:49.400
going to fly.

00:33:47.600 --> 00:33:51.400
>> What is like your approval rating for a

00:33:49.400 --> 00:33:53.960
franchisee, um just out of curiosity?

00:33:51.400 --> 00:33:56.640
>> So we do say no a lot more than we say

00:33:53.960 --> 00:33:59.640
yes. Whenever we identify any red flags,

00:33:56.640 --> 00:34:00.680
we're not going to award that franchise

00:33:59.640 --> 00:34:02.280
at all.

