>> Are morning routines underrated or

00:34:02.280 --> 00:34:06.320
overrated for entrepreneurs?

00:34:03.960 --> 00:34:09.080
>> Underrated. I think that rituals, your

00:34:06.320 --> 00:34:11.480
daily routine, that's that's everything.

00:34:09.080 --> 00:34:13.760
So that reflects for me personally from

00:34:11.480 --> 00:34:16.600
my daily workout as a ritual, from my

00:34:13.760 --> 00:34:18.560
daily nutrition to start my mornings,

00:34:16.600 --> 00:34:21.280
and then just how I start my day with

00:34:18.560 --> 00:34:23.200
the business. We have a team call to

00:34:21.280 --> 00:34:25.040
9:00 a.m. every day. The whole team is

00:34:23.200 --> 00:34:26.840
on it, and we just everyone just goes

00:34:25.040 --> 00:34:28.760
through what they accomplished the day

00:34:26.840 --> 00:34:30.919
before and what their focus is for the

00:34:28.760 --> 00:34:33.639
day, and it just kicks off the day the

00:34:30.919 --> 00:34:34.679
right way. So these daily rituals are

00:34:33.639 --> 00:34:36.360
everything.

00:34:34.679 --> 00:34:38.480
>> What's the worst no that you ever got,

00:34:36.360 --> 00:34:39.840
but how did that drive you forward?

00:34:38.480 --> 00:34:41.800
>> I think in the course of my career

00:34:39.840 --> 00:34:43.600
there's been a lot of no's. If it

00:34:41.800 --> 00:34:45.919
irritates you, like that could be a

00:34:43.600 --> 00:34:47.399
really a good thing that pushes you

00:34:45.919 --> 00:34:49.080
forward and helps you achieve your

00:34:47.399 --> 00:34:51.639
goals. Sometimes it's even your own

00:34:49.080 --> 00:34:53.159
family, right? When you first start out,

00:34:51.639 --> 00:34:54.720
you're taking a lot of risk. And if you

00:34:53.159 --> 00:34:56.040
come from a family that is used to

00:34:54.720 --> 00:34:58.080
playing it safe and having that

00:34:56.040 --> 00:35:00.400
corporate 9:00 to 5:00 job and valuing

00:34:58.080 --> 00:35:02.360
the stability, they can really influence

00:35:00.400 --> 00:35:03.160
you. So, you have to be very careful who

00:35:02.360 --> 00:35:05.000
you listen to.

00:35:03.160 --> 00:35:05.920
>> Do you need a Does an entrepreneur need

00:35:05.000 --> 00:35:07.240
to have that like chip on their

00:35:05.920 --> 00:35:08.840
shoulder? Like, I need to prove someone

00:35:07.240 --> 00:35:10.760
wrong? Or what's your take on that?

00:35:08.840 --> 00:35:12.200
>> I think sometimes for depending on

00:35:10.760 --> 00:35:14.160
mindset, like that chip could be

00:35:12.200 --> 00:35:15.560
helpful. I think the one thing that most

00:35:14.160 --> 00:35:17.520
entrepreneurs need is they need to have

00:35:15.560 --> 00:35:18.720
that hunger. They have to be hungry.

00:35:17.520 --> 00:35:20.080
They don't necessarily have to be like

00:35:18.720 --> 00:35:21.880
angry at the world and trying to prove

00:35:20.080 --> 00:35:23.960
something, although some situations can

00:35:21.880 --> 00:35:25.960
be helpful, but they definitely need

00:35:23.960 --> 00:35:27.960
that that hunger because that's going to

00:35:25.960 --> 00:35:30.920
be that drive to get there.

00:35:27.960 --> 00:35:32.960
>> Tell us about fire, ready, aim, and how

00:35:30.920 --> 00:35:34.680
that drives business results. Has moving

00:35:32.960 --> 00:35:36.680
too fast ever cost you?

00:35:34.680 --> 00:35:38.720
>> We see entrepreneurs and first-time

00:35:36.680 --> 00:35:40.640
founders struggle with analysis by

00:35:38.720 --> 00:35:41.960
paralysis. What ends up happening is

00:35:40.640 --> 00:35:44.120
they're they're doing their business

00:35:41.960 --> 00:35:46.440
plan, they're strategizing,

00:35:44.120 --> 00:35:48.800
and they never take action. They just

00:35:46.440 --> 00:35:50.440
keep refining it. All these delay

00:35:48.800 --> 00:35:52.480
happens, and by the time they're ready

00:35:50.440 --> 00:35:55.120
to take action, they missed the boat.

00:35:52.480 --> 00:35:58.160
And so, it's much better to just focus

00:35:55.120 --> 00:35:59.920
on execution. And just take action

00:35:58.160 --> 00:36:01.360
immediately. And it's okay to make

00:35:59.920 --> 00:36:03.400
mistakes. You're going to make mistakes,

00:36:01.360 --> 00:36:05.640
but as long as you course correct and

00:36:03.400 --> 00:36:08.800
get back on track, that's how that

00:36:05.640 --> 00:36:11.720
momentum is going to carry you through.

00:36:08.800 --> 00:36:14.040
So, the person who takes action first

00:36:11.720 --> 00:36:15.800
will run circles around the persons that

00:36:14.040 --> 00:36:17.160
that is strategizing. Wait, guys, we're

00:36:15.800 --> 00:36:18.080
not ready yet. We've got to focus on our

00:36:17.160 --> 00:36:19.680
strategy. We've got to write our

00:36:18.080 --> 00:36:21.560
business plan. The person who takes

00:36:19.680 --> 00:36:23.160
action first and gets started and gets

00:36:21.560 --> 00:36:25.000
that momentum going is going to run

00:36:23.160 --> 00:36:27.040
circles around that person who suffers

00:36:25.000 --> 00:36:28.320
from paralysis by analysis.

